fourier-spinners (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed Fourier.cpp to actually compile and spit out two chain objects
  * abandoning idea of creatin objects from Fourier.cpp's DFT function. Making
    commit for future reference
  * It runs again, but it sure as hell doesn't work. DFT isn't transforming.
    Comparing against older V2 build shows no difference in actual algorithm --
    just the new vars for vertical & horizonal values all in one go
  * Transform appears to be working. Horizontal signal components had their
    sin/cos multipliers swapped causing the horizontal spinner to functionally
    flip across its diagonal axis. Current default signal draws an
    approximation of a single period of a sine wave.
  * Drawing fully working and no longer flipped. I'm gonna lose my shit now,
    thanks. TIME FOR POLISH!
  * Line fading! Only it cycles every 255 points, rather than normalized across
    the entire path length.
  * Created .gitignore file to filter out Windows SDL_src. ALSO ADDED WINDOWS
    SUPPORT AWW YE
  * Un-fucked the drawing direction & scale. Direction was error in sqrt()
    parameter functions. Scale is attenuation because of undersampling (so up
    the DFT_DEPTH value)
  * Readme file, and a month-long pause made me forget what I was doing D:
  * Fixed double-free on Chain -- may still leak memory from Spinners. Its
    unclear how the pointer is deallocated
  * Refactored the Makefile, bashed the Windows Makefile, and the code is
    still a mess.

